+# Agent Note: Model request parent lineage
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-20-model-request-parent-lineage.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Session-backed subagents persist their immediate `parentSession`, but agent-loop model requests previously carried only the child `sessionId`. A gateway could keep each child sticky, yet it could not reconstruct root/child topology or attribute child inference to the owning trajectory without reading harness persistence.
+
+## Decision
+
+`GenerateOptions` carries an optional `parentSessionId` beside `sessionId`. The agent loop derives both values from the same durable Session header on every ordinary request, and compaction-basic does the same for its auxiliary summary request. Root sessions and hand-built direct calls omit parent identity unless their caller supplies it explicitly.
+
+The direct DeepSeek adapter sends the value as model-hidden `x-deepseek-harness-parent-session-id` whenever it is present, alongside the existing `x-deepseek-harness-session-id`. It does not infer lineage, mutate the request body, or read ambient agent state. The receiving gateway remains responsible for deciding whether and how to use this metadata.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+- **Infer lineage from session identifiers.** Session ids are opaque and carry no stable hierarchy, so parsing them would create a false contract.
+- **Route every child under the root session id.** This would erase per-child affinity and make concurrent child requests indistinguishable.
+- **Let the adapter query the agent registry.** Direct and auxiliary LLM calls are valid outside an agent loop. Keeping lineage in `GenerateOptions` preserves the adapter boundary and makes the transport fact explicit and testable.
+
+## Verification
+
+Agent-loop coverage creates a session-backed child and pins the exact child and parent ids received by its adapter. DeepSeek adapter coverage pins both native wire headers. Existing root and direct-call tests continue to omit the parent header.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Gateways can reconstruct immediate DSH trajectory lineage without inspecting model-visible content or harness storage, while root and standalone requests retain their old wire shape. `GenerateOptions` gains one transport-metadata field, and adapters other than the direct DeepSeek route may ignore it until they have a concrete host contract.
